>> title: Balsamic Fig Chicken with Roasted Potatoes & Mixed Greens
>> servings: 2
>> prep time: 10 minutes
>> cook time: 30 minutes
>> total time: 40 minutes
>> cuisine: American
>> course: dinner
>> tags: hellofresh, chicken, weeknight
>> source: HelloFresh WK 24-1
>> description: Pan-seared chicken cutlets with a sweet-tangy balsamic fig sauce, roasted Yukon Gold potatoes, and a lemony mixed-green salad. About 490 calories per serving.

Adjust the rack to the top position and preheat the oven to 450°F. For a hotter start, put the #baking sheet{} in the oven while it heats so the potatoes sizzle as soon as they land. Wash and dry all produce.

Dice @Yukon Gold potatoes{12%oz} into ½-inch pieces. Toss on the #baking sheet{} with @olive oil{2%tsp}, @kosher salt{}, and @black pepper{}. Roast on the top rack, tossing halfway through, until browned and tender, ~{20%minutes} to ~{25%minutes}.

While the potatoes roast, halve, peel, and mince @red onion{1} until you have 2 tablespoons. Save the rest of the onion for another use. Strip @rosemary{1%tsp} leaves from the stems and finely chop them. Halve @lemon{1}.

Pat @chicken cutlets{10%oz} dry with paper towels and season all over with @kosher salt{} and @black pepper{}. Heat @olive oil{1%tsp} in a #large pan{} over medium-high heat. Add the chicken and cook until browned and cooked through, ~{3%minutes} to ~{5%minutes} per side. Chicken is done at 165°F. Transfer it to a cutting board and lower the heat to medium.

Add the minced onion, chopped rosemary, and @olive oil{1%tsp} to the same pan. Cook, stirring, until softened, ~{2%minutes} to ~{3%minutes}. Stir in @balsamic vinegar{5%tsp} and @fig jam{2%tbsp}. Simmer until syrupy, ~{1%minute}. Stir in @chicken stock concentrate{1} and @water{0.25%cup}. Cook until thick and glossy, ~{2%minutes} to ~{3%minutes}. Add a splash of water if the sauce is too thick. Turn off the heat, stir in @butter{1%tbsp}, and season with @kosher salt{} and @black pepper{}.

While the sauce simmers, toss @mixed greens{2%oz} in a #medium bowl{} with a squeeze of lemon juice and a drizzle of @olive oil{}. Season with @kosher salt{} and @black pepper{}.

Thinly slice the chicken crosswise. Divide the chicken and potatoes between plates, drizzle the chicken with the balsamic fig sauce, and serve the salad on the side.

-- Four servings: 24 oz Yukon Gold potatoes, 1 red onion (mince 4 tablespoons), 1/2 oz rosemary (2 tsp chopped leaves), 1 lemon, 20 oz chicken cutlets, 10 tsp balsamic vinegar, 4 tbsp fig jam, 2 chicken stock concentrates, 4 oz mixed greens, 2 tbsp butter, and 1/3 cup water. The HelloFresh card lists 4 tsp olive oil for both yields.
-- Butter contains milk.
